{
  "_comment": "JSON-LD serialization of the BatteryPass rendering. Keys are the published BatteryPass attribute names; each expands to the IRI of that attribute in its own namespace. One BatteryPass data model, referenced through two renderings. (1) bpsamm-* = the Battery Pass Consortium SAMM aspect models (github.com/batterypass/BatteryPassDataModel), real published versions 1.2.0 (Performance 1.2.1); these match the skos mappings in battery.ttl and are the canonical form. (2) bpr: = an OpenEPCIS-hosted reference namespace for the few GEFEG BatteryPass-Ready longlist v1.3 attributes with no SAMM equivalent (the DPP-information group #1-#4); GEFEG (thebatterypass.eu / batterypass-ready.gefeg.com) is the Consortium's publication and validation channel and publishes no RDF IRIs. There is no SAMM 1.3.0 and no SAMM DPPInformation submodel.",
  "_direction": "This context does NOT translate eubat: IRIs into BatteryPass IRIs. A JSON-LD context maps a KEY to an IRI; it cannot redirect one IRI to another, which is what the previous revision attempted and why no processor could load it. To read an OpenEPCIS battery passport with BatteryPass keys, compact it with battery-context-batterypass-bridge.jsonld. To relate the two vocabularies as RDF, use the graded skos mappings carried in ontology/battery.ttl.",
  "@context": {
    "@version": 1.1,
    "gs1": "https://ref.gs1.org/voc/",
    "eubat": "https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/eu/battery/",
    "oec": "https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/",
    "xsd": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#",
    "bpsamm-general": "urn:samm:io.BatteryPass.GeneralProductInformation:1.2.0#",
    "bpsamm-perf": "urn:samm:io.BatteryPass.Performance:1.2.1#",
    "bpsamm-carbon": "urn:samm:io.BatteryPass.CarbonFootprint:1.2.0#",
    "bpsamm-material": "urn:samm:io.BatteryPass.MaterialComposition:1.2.0#",
